--- bindings
{"T": {"kind": "column", "column": "name", "type": "TEXT"}}
--- source
T IN ("a", "b")
--- expect
((CAST(`name` AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin = CAST('a' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin) OR (CAST(`name` AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin = CAST('b' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin))
===

### name: op.in.one-value.value-binding
--- note
A scalar value binding on the right is the same one value: EQL's rule, which casts it beside an exact column because it is not a text literal.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"A": {"kind": "column", "column": "value", "type": "TEXT", "exact": true}, "V": {"kind": "value", "value": "ab"}}
--- source
A IN V
--- expect
(`value` = CAST('ab' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin)
===

### name: op.in.one-value.value-binding.eql-twin
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"A": {"kind": "column", "column": "value", "type": "TEXT", "exact": true}, "V": {"kind": "value", "value": "ab"}}
--- source
A EQL V
--- expect
(`value` = CAST('ab' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin)
===

